{"type":"message","id":"9a898f6f","parentId":"8732d30c","timestamp":"2026-02-12T16:42:14.931Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_psUYCDgqfaC7R2GmBMasSkV2","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\docs\\AUTO-TESTS-SETUP.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-4o","usage":{"input":591,"output":48,"cacheRead":6912,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":7551,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770914533772}}
{"type":"message","id":"82d485b0","parentId":"9a898f6f","timestamp":"2026-02-12T16:42:14.971Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_psUYCDgqfaC7R2GmBMasSkV2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# GitHub Actions CI/CD Setup for Playwright Tests\n\nThis document explains how to set up and use GitHub Actions for running Playwright tests automatically.\n\n## Workflow Overview\n\nThe GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/playwright.yml`) is configured to:\n\n- **Trigger**: Run on pushes and pull requests to `main` and `develop` branches\n- **Environment**: Ubuntu latest with Node.js LTS\n- **Browsers**: Chromium with system dependencies\n- **Artifacts**: Upload test reports and results for 30 days\n\n## Workflow Steps\n\n1. **Checkout code** - Downloads your repository\n2. **Setup Node.js** - Installs Node.js LTS with npm caching\n3. **Install dependencies** - Runs `npm ci` for faster, reliable installs\n4. **Install Playwright browsers** - Installs Chromium with system dependencies\n5. **Run tests** - Executes all Playwright tests\n6. **Upload artifacts** - Saves test reports and results for debugging\n\n## Key Features\n\n### ✅ Modern Approach\n- Uses the **recommended Playwright CLI** approach instead of the deprecated GitHub Action\n- Based on [Microsoft's official documentation](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright-github-action)\n\n### ✅ Performance Optimized\n- **npm ci** for faster dependency installation\n- **Node.js caching** to speed up builds\n- **Single browser** (Chromium) for faster execution\n- **Parallel test execution** where possible\n\n### ✅ Robust Error Handling\n- **60-minute timeout** prevents hanging builds\n- **Artifact upload** on both success and failure\n- **Retry logic** for flaky tests (2 retries on CI)\n\n### ✅ Developer Friendly\n- **HTML reports** for easy debugging\n- **Test artifacts** available for download\n- **Clear step naming** for easy troubleshooting\n\n## Setup Instructions\n\n### 1. Repository Setup\n```bash\n# Ensure your repository has the following files:\n# - .github/workflows/playwright.yml\n# - package.json\n# - playwright.config.js\n# - tests/ directory with your test files\n```\n\n### 2. Push to GitHub\n```bash\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Add Playwright tests with GitHub Actions\"\ngit push origin main\n```\n\n### 3. Monitor Results\n- Go to your repository on GitHub\n- Click the \"Actions\" tab\n- View the workflow runs and results\n- Download artifacts if tests fail\n\n## Local Testing\n\nTest your CI setup locally:\n\n```bash\n# Install dependencies\nnpm ci\n\n# Install browsers with system dependencies (like CI)\nnpm run install:browsers\n\n# Run tests in CI mode\nnpm run test:ci\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Tests Fail in CI but Pass Locally\n- Check if your local server is running (CI doesn't have your local server)\n- Consider using `webServer` configuration in `playwright.config.js`\n- Verify environment variables and secrets\n\n### Common CI Issues\n- **Missing package-lock.json**: Run `npm install` locally to generate the lock file\n- **Artifact upload warnings**: The workflow uses `if-no-files-found: ignore` to handle empty directories gracefully\n- **Browser installation**: The workflow uses `--with-deps` flag for system dependencies\n\n### Browser Installation Fails\n- The workflow uses `--with-deps` flag for system dependencies\n- Check GitHub Actions logs for specific error messages\n- Ensure sufficient disk space in the runner\n\n### Timeout Issues\n- Increase timeout in workflow: `timeout-minutes: 120`\n- Optimize tests to run faster\n- Consider running fewer browsers in CI\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Keep tests fast** - CI should complete in under 10 minutes\n2. **Use specific selectors** - Avoid flaky tests\n3. **Test critical paths** - Focus on user journeys\n4. **Regular maintenance** - Update Playwright and dependencies\n5. **Monitor results** - Check CI runs regularly\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Playwright GitHub Action Documentation](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright-github-action)\n- [Playwright CI/CD Guide](https://playwright.dev/docs/ci)\n- [GitHub Actions Documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/actions)\n[ ] JButton AGILE TraceReady"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770914534968}}
{"type":"message","id":"d4d38b06","parentId":"82d485b0","timestamp":"2026-02-12T16:42:19.562Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mR4xilcBkr19uB56ToiUImtH","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\services\\aiConfigService.js","content":"// AI configuration service for dynamic provider selection\n\n// Import required modules (Axios, etc.)\nconst axios = require('axios');\nconst config = require('../config');\n\n// Possible providers\nconst Providers = {\n  VERCEL: 'vercel',\n  OPENROUTER: 'openrouter'\n};\n\n// Centralized configuration function\nconst getAIProvider = () => {\n  // Check configuration/environment variable for provider\n  const provider = config.aiProvider || process.env.AI_PROVIDER || Providers.VERCEL;\n\n  if (!Object.values(Providers).includes(provider)) {\n    throw new Error(`Invalid AI Provider: ${provider}`);\n  }\n\n  return provider;\n};\n\n// Abstract API function\nconst fetchAIResponse = async (endpoint, payload) => {\n  const provider = getAIProvider();\n  let url, headers;\n\n  switch (provider) {\n    case Providers.VERCEL:\n      url = `https://vercel-ai-api/${endpoint}`;\n      headers = { Authorization: `Bearer ${config.vercelApiKey}` };\n      break;\n    case Providers.OPENROUTER:\n      url = `https://openrouter-api/${endpoint}`;\n      headers = { Authorization: `Bearer ${config.openRouterApiKey}` };\n      break;\n    default:\n      throw new Error('Unsupported AI provider');\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const response = await axios.post(url, payload, { headers });\n    return response.data;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(`Error contacting ${provider} API:`, error.message);\n    throw error;\n  }\n};\n\nmodule.exports = { fetchAIResponse, Providers };"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-4o","usage":{"input":1024,"output":431,"cacheRead":7424,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8879,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770914534971}}
{"type":"message","id":"6a82bbc2","parentId":"d4d38b06","timestamp":"2026-02-12T16:42:19.599Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mR4xilcBkr19uB56ToiUImtH","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1430 bytes to C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\services\\aiConfigService.js"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770914539596}}
{"type":"message","id":"c967ef48","parentId":"6a82bbc2","timestamp":"2026-02-12T16:42:25.992Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2mdxTdGaHNo6JwI91lunQ633","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\tests\\aiConfigService.test.js","content":"const { fetchAIResponse, Providers } = require('../services/aiConfigService');\nconst axios = require('axios');\nconst config = require('../config');\n\njest.mock('axios');\n\ndescribe('AI Configuration Service', () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    jest.clearAllMocks();\n    config.aiProvider = undefined;\n    process.env.AI_PROVIDER = undefined;\n  });\n\n  test('should default to Vercel AI Gateway if no provider is specified', async () => {\n    config.vercelApiKey = 'vercel-api-key';\n    axios.post.mockResolvedValueOnce({ data: { success: true } });\n\n    const response = await fetchAIResponse('test-endpoint', { payload: true });\n\n    expect(axios.post).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n      'https://vercel-ai-api/test-endpoint',\n      { payload: true },\n      { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer vercel-api-key' } }\n    );\n    expect(response).toEqual({ success: true });\n  });\n\n  test('should use OpenRouter when configured', async () => {\n    config.aiProvider = Providers.OPENROUTER;\n    config.openRouterApiKey = 'openrouter-api-key';\n    axios.post.mockResolvedValueOnce({ data: { success: true } });\n\n    const response = await fetchAIResponse('test-endpoint', { payload: true });\n\n    expect(axios.post).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n      'https://openrouter-api/test-endpoint',\n      { payload: true },\n      { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer openrouter-api-key' } }\n    );\n    expect(response).toEqual({ success: true });\n  });\n\n  test('should throw an error for unsupported providers', async () => {\n    config.aiProvider = 'unsupported';\n\n    await expect(fetchAIResponse('test-endpoint', { payload: true }))\n      .rejects\n      .toThrow('Invalid AI Provider: unsupported');\n  });\n\n  test('should handle API errors gracefully', async () => {\n    config.aiProvider = Providers.VERCEL;\n    config.vercelApiKey = 'vercel-api-key';\n    axios.post.mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error('API Error'));\n\n    await expect(fetchAIResponse('test-endpoint', { payload: true }))\n      .rejects\n      .toThrow('API Error');\n\n    expect(axios.post).toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n});"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-4o","usage":{"input":474,"output":625,"cacheRead":8448,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9547,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770914539600}}
